---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout title="About" description="About this quietly modern Twenty Ten-inspired demo weblog.">
  <article>
    <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
    <div class="post-content">
      <p>This is a fictional demo notebook for software, systems, and the details worth remembering.</p>
      <p>The design keeps the calm, text-first character of WordPress Twenty Ten while the site underneath is static Astro: Markdown files, durable URLs, and very little client-side JavaScript.</p>
      <h2 id="colophon">Colophon</h2>
      <p>Typeset with system fonts, highlighted by Shiki, and built as plain HTML and CSS. Its proportions and header treatment faithfully follow the original Twenty Ten theme.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
